## Approach

Standalone `LessonsDb` struct with its own rusqlite connection to `~/.sutra/lessons.db`, its own migration runner (modeled on `Db::run_migrations` but independent), the `sutra_remember` MCP tool for write, and lesson injection into `sutra_read` responses via exact symbol-name anchor matching. The DB is opened once at server startup and shared across workspaces as `Arc<LessonsDb>` on `SutraServer`.

Why not extend `Db`? Lessons are cross-workspace (one global store), while `Db` is per-workspace. A separate struct with its own connection avoids coupling lessons to any single workspace's lifecycle, migration chain, or reindex behavior.

